# Every file tracked here is text, so normalise line endings to LF in the
# repository and check them out as LF on every platform. Without this, a
# contributor whose git has core.autocrlf=true checks the tree out as CRLF and
# then sees whole-file diffs on anything they touch.
#
# text=auto still detects a genuinely binary file and leaves it alone, so no
# per-extension binary rules are needed. The game assets this tool reads are
# never committed; .gitignore blocks them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Python-aware hunk headers, so a diff says which function it is in.
*.py diff=python
